# Lumbering Laundry: "{2}: Until end of turn, you may look at face-down creatures you don't control any time" (CR 611.2a, 708.5).
# Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Laundry off a Black Lotus and a Sol Ring. Turn 2 Bot2 casts Vengeful Creeper face down for its disguise.
# Turn 3 Bot1 knows nothing of it until the ability resolves, and then knows it is Vengeful Creeper, as its client draws it.
# The turn over, Bot1 can no longer look (the ruling): on turn 4 the Creeper is hidden from Bot1 again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Lumbering Laundry
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Vengeful Creeper
Forest x20

